---
import '../styles/global.css';

const { title = 'Takala Wang — Resume', lang = 'zh-Hant' } = Astro.props;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang={lang}>
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={lang === 'en' ? 'Takala Wang — Software Engineer and AI Researcher.' : '王重鈞的工程師履歷與作品集。'} />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <script is:inline>if (localStorage.getItem('resume-theme') === 'dark') document.documentElement.classList.add('dark'); else document.documentElement.classList.remove('dark');</script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <!--
      THESIS: A resume that reads like a finished product surface: the person leads, the work is selectable, and the evidence stays in one clear path. It refuses the portfolio card wall and the decorative hero.
      OWN-WORLD: SmoothUI-native rounded surfaces, quiet blue signals, crisp ink, compact rows, and one active work stage; no stars, glass cards, gradients, or slide-deck framing.
      STORY: Meet Takala, understand his current role, inspect five shipped systems through one live work surface, scan the timeline and technical profile, then contact him.
      FIRST VIEWPORT: Name, role, contact paths, and a current-profile surface share the opening field; the work section begins immediately after the education proof strip.
      FORM: SmoothUI product surface with an arcade-screen discipline for active states / direction seed 29aa9b12, assigned grounded candidate 3, code-led because real resume data and native controls are the product truth.
      FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
    -->
    <slot />
    <script is:inline>
      document.querySelectorAll('a[href^="#"]').forEach((link) => link.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (document.activeElement instanceof HTMLElement) document.activeElement.blur();
      }));
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
